detResDeg -- compute a regularity index and partial degrees of the determinantal resultant
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        detResDeg(n, c, r, R)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,  corresponding to the drop of
        rank used to form the determinantal resultant
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of degrees indexing the
        columns of a polynomial matrix
      * r, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of degrees indexing the
        rows of the same polynomial
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,  an ambient ring where the
        computations take place
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of element consisting of a
        regularity index and partial degree of homogeneity of the
        determinantal resultant

Description
===========


 Compute the regularity index and the multi-degree of the determinantal
resultant associated to the matrix M
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[d1,d2,d3,k1,k2]                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : detResDeg(1,{d1,d2,d3},{k1,k2},R)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {d1 + d2 + d3 - k1 - 2k2 - 1, {d2 + d3 - k1 - k2, d1 + d3 - k1 - k2, d1 |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     + d2 - k1 - k2}}                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

