eliminationMatrix(ZZ,List,Matrix) -- returns a matrix corresponding to the determinantal resultant, in particular the Macaulay resultant
****************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note eliminationMatrix: eliminationMatrix,
  * Usage: 
        eliminationMatrix(r, v, m)
  * Inputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, corresponding to the regularity
        index used to form the determinantal resultant
      * v, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,,  a list of homogeneous variables
        that are to be eliminated
      * m, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a polynomial matrix
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: eliminationMatrix, => ..., default value null, returns
        a matrix that represents the image of the map
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix corresponding to the
        determinantal resultant

Description
===========


 Compute the determinantal resultant of an (n,m)-matrix (n<m) of homogeneous
polynomials over the projective space of dimension (m-r)(n-r), i.e. a condition
on the parameters of these polynomials to have rank(M)<r+1.M
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[a_0..a_5,b_0..b_5,x,y]                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M:=matrix{{a_0*x+a_1*y,a_2*x+a_3*y,a_4*x+a_5*y},{b_0*x+b_1*y,b_2*x+b_3*y|
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | a_0x+a_1y a_2x+a_3y a_4x+a_5y |                                       |
|     | b_0x+b_1y b_2x+b_3y b_4x+b_5y |                                       |
|                                                                             |
|             2      3                                                        |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|,b_4*x+b_5*y}}                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : eliminationMatrix(1,{x,y},M, Strategy => determinantal)                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {2} | -a_2b_0+a_0b_2               -a_4b_0+a_0b_4                       |
|     {2} | -a_3b_0-a_2b_1+a_1b_2+a_0b_3 -a_5b_0-a_4b_1+a_1b_4+a_0b_5         |
